Fix WAL replay dropping jobs at max-job-size (issue #82; upstream bug, unfixed
in v1.13 and on master).

put accepts a body of up to job_data_size_limit bytes and stores the job with
body_size + 2, the body plus its trailing CRLF. readrec() and readrec5()
compared that stored size against job_data_size_limit itself, so on restart a
job whose body was max-job-size or max-job-size - 1 bytes was reported as
"too big", and the Error path stopped reading the rest of that binlog file,
dropping every later job in it.

Allow for the CRLF in the replay check. A stored record larger than a legal
put could have written is still rejected. The record format is unchanged, so
binlogs written before this fix replay correctly.

Oversized records under a smaller restart limit (issue #112): the rejection
above used to jump to Error before the framed body was read, so replay stopped
at the oversized record and silently dropped every later job in the same
binlog. The oversized case is always a full record (!j, so namelen is
nonzero) and its body length is known, so instead skip exactly jr.body_size
bytes and return success to replay the next record. The job is still not
created and the "too big" warning is still emitted. A truncated or corrupt
body (negative size, seek failure, or body past end of file) still takes the
Error path and stops replay of that file. No body-sized allocation is made.
--- a/file.c
+++ b/file.c
@@ -223,12 +223,28 @@
     case Buried:
     case Delayed:
         if (!j) {
-            if ((size_t)jr.body_size > job_data_size_limit) {
+            /* body_size includes the trailing CRLF that put stores after a
+             * body of up to job_data_size_limit bytes. */
+            if ((size_t)jr.body_size > job_data_size_limit + 2) {
+                off_t cur, end;
                 warnpos(f, -r, "job %"PRIu64" is too big (%"PRId32" > %zu)",
                         jr.id,
                         jr.body_size,
                         job_data_size_limit);
-                goto Error;
+                /* Framed full record: skip the body so replay continues with
+                 * the next record in this file. Treat a truncated or
+                 * unreadable body as an error and stop this file. */
+                cur = lseek(f->fd, 0, SEEK_CUR);
+                end = lseek(f->fd, 0, SEEK_END);
+                if (cur == (off_t)-1 || end == (off_t)-1 || cur > end ||
+                    jr.body_size < 0 ||
+                    (uint64_t)(end - cur) < (uint64_t)jr.body_size)
+                    goto Error;
+                /* SEEK_END moved the offset, so skip from the probed
+                 * offset rather than relative to the current one. */
+                if (lseek(f->fd, cur + jr.body_size, SEEK_SET) == (off_t)-1)
+                    goto Error;
+                return 1;
             }
             t = tube_find_or_make(tubename);
             j = make_job_with_id(jr.pri, jr.delay, jr.ttr, jr.body_size,
